// (xm 2^xe)^(yn 2^ye / yd) correctly rounded, for a power that is no Float
// and no midpoint of two and lies within 2^±1200: Ziv's strategy on
// __pow_fixed, doubling the width until both ends of its error interval
// round alike. CORE-MATH pow.c settles every Float base and exponent at
// 2^-240.07 relative error, so pow decides by 320; past 1024 bits, the
// width __LN2_1024 allows, the approximation's own rounding is returned.
__pow_ziv: fn(xm: Int, xe: Int, yn: Int, ye: Int, yd: Int) -> Float Never! {
    w := 160
